diff --git a/docs/OPENAI-STANDARD-BILLING.md b/docs/OPENAI-STANDARD-BILLING.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2fa1aa5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/OPENAI-STANDARD-BILLING.md
@@ -0,0 +1,88 @@
+# OpenAI standard quota policy
+
+`OPENAI_STANDARD_BILLING_ENABLED=true` activates the approved site quota policy
+`openai-standard-2026-10-30`. This is the site's quota schedule, not a guarantee
+of the upstream account's invoice or discounts. No balances are changed by this
+patch. Existing PKCE, identity binding and private per-user credential guards
+remain required.
+
+## Scope and configuration
+
+The policy covers exact model IDs `gpt-6-luna`, `gpt-6.1-terra`, and
+`gpt-6.1-sol` on an OpenAI channel using the official default URL,
+`https://api.openai.com`, or `https://api.openai.com/v1`. Only native Chat
+Completions and Responses requests are supported. Other endpoints in this
+scope fail before sending upstream. Other models, channel types and base URLs
+retain their existing billing behavior.
+
+For these three official-direct models, an unset/false feature flag deliberately
+fails closed even if legacy price maps are configured. Do not use flag=false as
+a return to static billing. Deploy/recover with this policy enabled; if access
+must be suspended, disable the Chat OAuth relay rather than rolling back to an
+older billing binary or restoring an older balance database.
+
+The selected channel/model is checked again immediately before the adapter
+sends a request. Model mapping, another selected channel, passthrough, a proxy,
+parameter/header overrides, service-tier forwarding, and Chat-to-Responses
+conversion are rejected for this policy. Request service tier must be absent
+or `default`. Chat cache-control TTL must be `30m`; ambiguous Chat `12h`
+breakpoints are rejected instead of being charged as `30m`.
+
+## Rates and calculation
+
+Sources checked 2026-10-30: [official pricing](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/pricing),
+the three official model pages, Chat/Responses usage schemas and prompt caching
+documentation. USD per 1,000,000 tokens:
+
+| Model | Ordinary input | Output | Cache read | Cache write 30m | Cache write 12h |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| gpt-6-luna | 0.10 | 0.50 | 0.01 | 0.125 | 0.25 |
+| gpt-6.1-terra | 1.00 | 5.00 | 0.05 | 1.25 | 2.50 |
+| gpt-6.1-sol | 2.00 | 10.00 | 0.10 | 2.50 | 5.00 |
+
+Input total `P` includes cache read and writes. Ordinary input is
+`P - cache_read - write_30m - write_12h`; writes are not charged twice.
+When actual `P > 272000`, all input/cache rates multiply by 2 and the output
+rate by 1.5 for the entire request. Exactly 272000 uses short-context rates.
+The resulting dollar amount multiplies by the native quota-per-dollar value
+and group ratio snapshotted at reservation. Existing native tool surcharges
+are retained, then the total is rounded once to the nearest quota unit
+(nonempty token usage has a minimum of one unit).
+
+Native base ratio maps may be populated for the original pricing display; they
+do not replace this policy. Display metadata explicitly describes the 30m/12h
+write tiers and long-context threshold; Claude 5m/1h fields are not repurposed.
+
+## Reservation, usage and failures
+
+The native preconsume/settlement path is retained. Reservation conservatively
+uses the highest supported input/write and long-context rates, with the stated
+output cap when available. This is a reservation, not the final charge:
+settlement refunds the excess. A very small balance can therefore be rejected
+before a short request whose actual final cost would have fit.
+
+Core input/output/total usage fields must be present, nonnegative integers and
+consistent. Optional cache counters default to zero when omitted. Responses
+with cache writes require an explicit 30m/12h breakdown matching total writes.
+Explicit all-zero usage is accepted only when no generated content is present.
+No missing usage is replaced with a local token estimate or a zero charge.
+
+Chat streaming always requests upstream usage while preserving the client's
+output preference. Identical duplicate usage snapshots are validated once,
+never accumulated; conflicting snapshots fail. Responses `completed` and
+`incomplete` terminal events with valid usage both settle normally. A missing,
+invalid or interrupted terminal usage produces `openai_standard_usage_unsettled`,
+skips automatic retries, follows native reservation refund/error auditing, and
+does not record a successful zero-cost request. A streaming error is sent using
+the corresponding Chat or Responses error protocol. This cannot prove whether
+the provider billed an interrupted request; operator reconciliation may be
+needed. Logs contain bounded reason codes and counts, not raw requests or keys.
+
+## Offline verification
+
+Tests use synthetic payloads and a transport that never opens a network socket.
+They cover fixed rate fixtures, cache partitions, exact threshold boundaries,
+price/group snapshots, endpoint and feature-off guards, unrelated channels,
+nonstream/stream usage, valid incomplete responses, missing/conflicting usage,
+client usage hiding and protocol-visible streaming errors. No paid upstream
+request or real-invoice parity test is included.
